          <output>`Task.run` on `A03_AuthorPages` executed. Summary:

**What ran** — `A03_AuthorPages` is an `InstructionTask`, so `execute()` ran its `instructions` once.

**Findings** — the corpus already had all 25 A02 pages copied into A03 (`page.docs.*`, physically under `a03_authoring/data_IGNORE/`), each already carrying a full semantic scaffold (`authoritativeSources`, `learningObjectives`, `readerOutcomes`, `scopes`, `exclusions`, `content`) that follows the `PageExample_A03` pattern. `BmlDocSet_A03.pages`/`homePage`, all 10 A03 `PageGroups`, and the `Library` catalog exports (pages, groups, DocSet, tasks) were also already correct from prior operations in this transform (#1, #2) — no additions/removals/exports needed.

**Verification against A02** (script-compared all 25 pages):
- `title`, `pageType`, `detailLevel`, `isNot` — already matched A02 exactly.
- `is` (20/25 pages) and `purpose` (all 25 pages) — did **not** match A02 verbatim; the existing A03 content had paraphrased these instead of carrying them over as required by step 4 (&quot;set `is`/override `purpose` from the A02 page&quot;). Fixed all 25 by copying the exact A02 `&lt;is>` and `&lt;purpose>` blocks into the A03 files, leaving the already-authored semantic scaffold untouched.
- `authoritativeSources` selectors across all pages resolve only to `org.blockml.bml.core.*` / `org.blockml.bml.documentation.*` — within the allowed whitelist, no cross-sector leakage.
- No `&lt;code>` left on any `CodeBlock`; every content page has a `Requires` see-link; `TableOfContents` (Index page) has a pure `Navigation` tree targeting only A03 pages.
- No A03 page references an A01/A02/A04 Block (the only a01/a02 mentions found are prose text in `PageGroup`/`BmlDocSet_A03` documentation, and a pre-existing `pdata:BmlDocSetPlan` see-link on `BmlDocSet_A03` — both owned by `A03_CopyDocSet`, outside this task's scope).

**Validation** — `blockml validate --all`: 641 blocks, 0 errors (unchanged).

**Changed files** (unstaged, not committed) — the 25 files under `packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a03_authoring/data_IGNORE/page/docs/`, `is`/`purpose` text only.

As with the prior two operations in this transform, I haven't touched the running transform record or made a commit — flipping operation #3 to `Succeeded` and committing appears to be a separate step outside this task's scope.
</output>
